1. A printing press suction system comprising:

a support structure configured to be mounted in a printing press;

a plurality of suction boxes carried by the support structure, the suction boxes being arranged adjacent to one another and each extending transversely relative to a direction of travel of a substrate through the printing press;

at least one suction source fluidly connectable to the plurality of suction boxes; and

a plurality of releasable connections respectively associated with the suction boxes,

wherein each suction box is independently removable from the support structure while at least one adjacent suction box remains mounted to the support structure.
